<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adonijah</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adonijah was the fourth son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">King David</a> according to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Hebrew Bible</a>. As the eldest surviving son, he claimed the throne in David's old age with the support of the commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joab">Joab</a> and the priest Abiathar, but the prophet Nathan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bathsheba">Bathsheba</a> persuaded David to name <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a> king instead, and Solomon later had Adonijah put to death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/adonijah.jpg" alt="Adonijah" width="320" height="368" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymous Russian manuscript illuminators, 1560-1570s Facial Chronicle (Illustrated Chronicle of Ivan the Terrible) (... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Facial_Chronicle_-_b.03,_p.172_-_David_with_sons_in_Hebron.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
